From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: soc: sunxi: cpu_comm: a start that timed out closes the call path again

cpu_comm_firmware_start() gives the count back before it waits for READY,
so a core that never answered left the call path open and
cpu_comm_firmware_up() said "up". That word is what keeps the HDMI
receiver's LINK poll off a dead block (0236/0237): on 08.10.2026 one such
read held the bus and the watchdog reset the device. After the timeout the
stop's count is taken again (fw_down), the next stop finds it taken and
takes no second one, and the next start gives it back as before. Review of
09.10.2026, CC-1 (arbeit/review-r2-20261009/FUNDE.md).

Not measured at the device: needs a restart that times out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Mythos 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/cpu_comm/cpu_comm_dev.c
@@ -1388,6 +1388,20 @@
 	if (!ret) {
 		WRITE_ONCE(mips_app_ready_assumed, 1);
 		pr_info("cpu_comm: the coprocessor is ready after %u ms\n", waited);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * A core that never answered is not up: the call path closes
+		 * again and cpu_comm_firmware_up() says so, so that nobody
+		 * (the receiver's LINK poll, 0236/0237) reads a block whose
+		 * core is dead and hangs the bus. The next stop finds the
+		 * count taken and takes no second one (review 09.10., CC-1).
+		 */
+		mutex_lock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
+		if (!cpu_comm_fw_down) {
+			cpu_comm_fw_down = true;
+			cpu_comm_suspend(0);
+		}
+		mutex_unlock(&cpu_comm_call_mutex);
 	}
 	blocking_notifier_call_chain(&cpu_comm_fw_chain,
 				     CPU_COMM_FIRMWARE_STARTED, &ret);
@@ -2403,10 +2417,21 @@
  * the noirq phase whatever the runtime references say, and the MIPS polls
  * its HDMI-RX PHY in TVCAP. Standby to RAM parks it first, below.
  */
+/*
+ * The software state before the register: a core parked by an earlier
+ * sleep or stopped for a restart is no core to refuse for or to park, and
+ * after a raw park the MIPS block sits behind a closed bus gate, where a
+ * read of its status word would hang the bus (review 09.10., CC-6).
+ */
+static bool cpu_comm_mips_gone(void)
+{
+	return READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_parked_since) || READ_ONCE(cpu_comm_fw_down);
+}
+
 static int cpu_comm_prepare(struct device *dev)
 {
 	if (pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_TO_IDLE ||
-	    !cpu_comm_mips_running())
+	    cpu_comm_mips_gone() || !cpu_comm_mips_running())
 		return 0;
 	dev_err(dev, "s2idle would power TVFE/TVCAP off under the running display coprocessor, refused\n");
 	return -EOPNOTSUPP;
@@ -2427,7 +2452,7 @@
 	if (pm_suspend_target_state != PM_SUSPEND_MEM)
 		return 0;
 	cpu_comm_s2r_count++;
-	if (!cpu_comm_mips_running()) {
+	if (cpu_comm_mips_gone() || !cpu_comm_mips_running()) {
 		/*
 		 * Parked since an earlier sleep, or held after a restart that
 		 * failed past its park: the pipeline the old firmware set up
